; One side of the NRL rules' contexts (two of these run, one reading leftwards and one rightwards). It takes in a
; word (its letters' codes, then the end card, from loader) into cells 85 on, after the edge at 84, with an edge
; (28) after it. Then for each letter, two cards from loader: where to start (as the word CLA cell) and which way
; (-1 or 1); -1 instead ends the word. Then for each rule, from rule.cq, the rule's elements on this side, up to 0;
; out, 1 if each matches in turn, else 0; -1 from rule.cq instead says the rule matched, on to the next letter. An element is three cards: how many (1 exactly one; 10 none or more, 11
; one or more, 12 two or more: q - 10 at least) and the range of codes it takes, lo to hi. Cells are read through
; the word at rw, moved by dir.
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            word    CLA   wst      03-16: a word into 85 on, and the edge after it
  04                    STO   sw
  05            gw      INP   x
  06                    CLA   x
  07                    TAC   endw
  08            sw      DATA  0        (STO 85 + n)
  09                    CLA   sw
  10                    ADD   00
  11                    STO   sw
  12                    JMP   gw
  13            endw    CLA   sw
  14                    STO   se
  15                    CLA   c28
  16            se      DATA  0        (STO the edge after the word)
  17            lett    INP   p0       17-20: a letter: where to start and which way, or the word's end
  18                    CLA   p0
  19                    TAC   word
  20            gdir    INP   dir
  21            rule    CLA   00       21-84: a rule's elements on this side, and the verdict
  22                    STO   ok
  23                    CLA   p0
  24                    STO   pw
  25            el      INP   q
  26                    CLA   q
  27                    TAC   lett
  28                    SUB   00
  29                    TAC   verd
  30                    INP   lo
  31                    INP   hi
  32                    CLA   ok
  33                    SUB   00
  34                    TAC   el
  35                    CLA   q
  36                    SUB   c10
  37                    STO   need
  38            rep     CLA   pw
  39                    STO   rw
  40            rw      DATA  0        (CLA a cell of the word)
  41                    STO   v
  42                    SUB   lo
  43                    TAC   miss
  44                    CLA   hi
  45                    SUB   v
  46                    TAC   miss
  47                    CLA   pw
  48                    ADD   dir
  49                    STO   pw
  50                    CLA   need
  51                    SUB   00
  52                    STO   need
  53                    CLA   q
  54                    SUB   n2
  55                    TAC   el
  56                    JMP   rep
  57            miss    CLA   q
  58                    SUB   n2
  59                    TAC   fail
  60                    CLA   z
  61                    SUB   need
  62                    TAC   fail
  63                    JMP   el
  64            fail    CLA   z
  65                    STO   ok
  66                    JMP   el
  67            verd    OUT   ok
  68                    JMP   rule
  69            x       DATA  0
  70            p0      DATA  0
  71            dir     DATA  0
  72            ok      DATA  0
  73            pw      DATA  0
  74            q       DATA  0
  75            lo      DATA  0
  76            hi      DATA  0
  77            need    DATA  0
  78            v       DATA  0
  79            z       DATA  0
  80            n2      DATA  2
  81            c10     DATA  10
  82            c28     DATA  28
  83            wst     STO   85
  84            edge    DATA  28
